From 660534d5e79b92d5510e4f11c64f140ef0e8d63c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:12:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AmgX: nodal blocks, symmetric cycle of the aggregation
 multigrid

The aggregation multigrid of the default configurations of AmgX was the
one of the configuration PCG_AGGREGATION_JACOBI of AmgX: three
post-smoothing sweeps of a Jacobi smoother damped by 0.8, no
pre-smoothing sweep. It does not converge on the linear elasticity (the
conjugate gradients stall or break down, also with a symmetric cycle
damped by 0.8). It is now one sweep damped by 0.6 before and after the
coarse correction, a symmetric cycle: 141 iterations of the conjugate
gradient on the beam of 56,355 unknowns of the benchmark, 271 with stiff
inclusions, and 31 instead of 26 on the Laplace equation, each cycle being
cheaper.

The option NodalBlocks gives the matrices and the vectors to AmgX by
square blocks of the size of the number of components of the unknowns,
ordered by vector dimension (block compressed rows built in O(nnz),
sequential and distributed uploads). The classical multigrid of AmgX does
not support blocks: the option requires the aggregation multigrid or a
configuration given. On the beam, the nodal blocks do not reduce the
iterations of the aggregation multigrid (151 against 141).

AmgXSolverTest checks the refusals, that the block Jacobi preconditioner
of AmgX on the nodal blocks is NodalBlockJacobi (sequential: in parallel,
the smoothers of AmgX 2.5 used alone return a null correction with
blocks), that a resolution by AmgX of the system given by blocks satisfies
the system of MFEM, and the convergence of the aggregation multigrid on
the linear elasticity, with and without blocks.
